WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.737
The common table expression creates patient-level features.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:10.997
Inside it, correlated scalar subqueries calculate each patient's admission count, abnormal-lab count,

00:00:10.997 --> 00:00:16.992
and distinct-medication count. The outer SELECT then calculates the synthetic score.

00:00:16.992 --> 00:00:22.612
When reading a long query, identify the row grain and feature columns first.

00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:25.442
Only then interpret the final derived expression.

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:28.622
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:28.622 --> 00:00:36.092
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:36.092 --> 00:00:38.052
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:38.052 --> 00:00:44.027
In a real setting such as a compliance workflow checking whether related evidence exists,

00:00:44.027 --> 00:00:51.732
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:51.732 --> 00:00:54.587
before discussing syntax.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:01:00.760
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
